{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The charge stands or falls on POL-NS-01(c): the driver must have held position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous dwell of at least 300 seconds for a LARGE_VENUE pickup. On the platform's own derived figures the longest continuous qualifying run is 170 seconds — the first interval in the bay runs 19:00:00 to 19:02:50 and the second 19:03:50 to 19:06:30. Neither interval, taken on its own, comes close to the 300-second minimum, so limb (c) is not satisfied by the driver's actual, continuous conduct.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The two intervals are genuinely separate because the driver left the bay between them: the trace records a 60-second excursion from 19:02:50 to 19:03:50 in which the driver reached 179.8 m from the pickup pin and was recorded at 24 km/h — travelling during the waiting period, not holding position. A wait broken by a 60-second, roughly 180-metre departure is not the unbroken hold that POL-NS-01(c) requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.excursions",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the rider's case the effective in-geofence dwell is the 170-second continuous run — 130 seconds short of the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum — and POL-NS-06 then provides that the cancellation fee is 'not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages'. The rider's own device sitting 519 m from the pin, and the absence of any rider message in the chat log, are therefore immaterial to this clause and cannot be used to prop up the charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-TRIP-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_run_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only figure that reaches 300 seconds is the accumulated 330 seconds, and that figure exists solely because POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed where a qualifying traffic advisory made holding position unlawful. That provision is a computation rule for the shortfall test in POL-NS-06; it does not enact a continuous dwell, and the continuous-dwell condition in POL-NS-01(c) remains a separate condition of chargeability. The advisory in force — a MODERATE kerb closure whose own description tells vehicles to 'circulate before returning to the marked bay' — explains why the driver left, but it does not convert two short waits into a single 300-second hold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-ADVIS-09107-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.accumulated_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own account corroborates a broken wait rather than a continuous hold: he messaged at 19:02:30 that the kerb was temporarily closed and that he 'must circulate and will return to the same bay', and again at 19:04:05 that he was 'back at the marked bay now'. That is the same 60-second departure the trace shows, and it is inconsistent with an unbroken 300-second hold in the bay.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09107", "EV-GPS-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Compensation to the driver can only follow a POL-NS-01 that is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-07 says so expressly. Where the effective dwell falls short, POL-NS-06 provides that the full refund stands and no driver compensation is payable. The rider therefore asks that the SGD 4.00 charged be returned and that nothing be paid to the driver out of it, the fare record confirming the fee was charged and not reversed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties' accounts and the platform telemetry agree on the sequence at the Orchard Central marked ride-hail bay. The driver arrived about 19:00, the platform logged 'arrived' at 19:00:20, a kerb closure (EV-ADVIS-09107-01, type CLOSURE, active 18:50-19:30, geometry covering the pickup road and window covering the wait) forced one short circulation from 19:02:50 to 19:03:50 - peaking 179.8 m from the pin - and he returned to the same bay at 19:04:05, remaining until he cancelled at 19:06:30 with RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nThe rider is right on the raw facts: the two in-bay stretches (170 s from 19:00:00 to 19:02:50, and 160 s from 19:03:50 to 19:06:30) are each far short of the 300 s LARGE_VENUE minimum, and POL-NS-01(c) speaks of a continuous dwell. But POL-NS-06(i) is the provision that governs how dwell is counted where a qualifying traffic advisory made holding position unlawful: it expressly permits separate in-geofence intervals within a single pickup attempt to be summed, provided the driver never travelled more than 300 m from the pin. Both conditions are met - the advisory is present and populated with an admissible type (CLOSURE) and covers the pickup road and the waiting period, and the driver's furthest point was 179.8 m, inside the 300 m leash. The intervals therefore accumulate to 330 s, 30 s above the 300 s minimum, and there is no shortfall for POL-NS-06 to refund. The rider's central argument - that POL-NS-06(i) is merely a computation rule for the shortfall test and cannot satisfy POL-NS-01(c) - is rejected: it is precisely the rule that makes the summed time count towards the POL-NS-01 minimum, and reading it the other way would leave the fee neither chargeable under POL-NS-01 nor refundable under POL-NS-06. The rider's related points (the 60-second, 179.8 m, 24 km/h excursion and the driver's own chat messages at 19:02:30 and 19:04:05 describing the circulation) are accepted as facts but do not defeat aggregation.\n\nThe remaining conditions of chargeability hold. Thirty-five qualifying fixes at 25 m accuracy or better place the driver inside the 120 m arrival radius before the arrived event, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied and the dispute turns on dwell. There is no false-arrival marker: the arrived event is 20 s after the first qualifying in-geofence fix and nothing is near the 300 m or 15 km/h triggers (POL-NS-05). The termination limb is met: no boarding event and a driver cancellation coded RIDER_NO_SHOW at 19:06:30, after the minimum elapsed (POL-NS-01(d)). The fee reconciles with the schedule - the greater of the LARGE_VENUE 4.00 and RYDE_X 4.00 is 4.00, matching the fare line - so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. No POL-NS-04 exoneration applies: the rider sent no locating or coordinating message, and her device sat about 519 m from the pin throughout the wait, outside the 150 m rider-presence radius. POL-NS-03 does not apply either, because the driver did hold position inside the arrival radius, and with registered_pickup_points at 1 the pin-ambiguity goodwill of POL-NS-03(ii) is not available.\n\nThe SGD 4.00 fee therefore stands and the rider's claim is not supported. Because the charge stands, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee: SGD 3.20. The anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination in 30 days, below the threshold of 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below 0.08), so compensation is paid rather than withheld. No escalation trigger is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict on arrival, dwell or rider presence, neither profile shows counterparty disputes in the trailing 90 days, the anti-farming check did not trip and rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and no deciding artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 (no clock skew, no trace gap, complete chat against chat_message_count of 3, and a reconciling fare line). All artifacts carry weight 1.0, so confidence is capped at 1.0. No clause produces a referral: POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged and the POL-NS-07 escalation direction is not triggered."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
